{"abstract": "Training a machine learning (ML) model is an optimization process that typically requires a set of examples with ground-truth labels beforehand. Obtaining these ground truths usually requires laborious human effort and can be costly. The scalability of human labeling becomes a concern when there are a large number of data points that need to be labeled. To address this practical issue, we consider an optimization setting where a subset of samples has ground-truth labels, while the remaining data points were labeled by an ML predictor, which could potentially assign incorrect labels to those points. We propose both first-order and zeroth-order stochastic optimization methods for training on datasets consisting of a mix of true-labeled and ML-labeled samples. We further conduct comprehensive empirical studies from training a linear regression model to fine-tuning a large language model (LLM) to showcase the effectiveness of the proposed algorithms for training with ML-labeled data.", "authors": ["Maria-Eleni Sfyraki", "Jun-Kun Wang"], "candidate_id": "7229499f7f76fe2e28f08e50", "decision": "summarize", "doi": "10.48550/arxiv.2610.26790", "landing_page": "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2610.26790", "mandatory": false, "matched_projects": ["zeroth-order-optimization"], "open_access_url": "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2610.26790", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/W7223016913", "schema_version": 1, "score": 0.76, "score_breakdown": [{"contribution": 0.32, "evidence": ["confirmed"], "feature": "project_confidence"}, {"contribution": 0.1, "evidence": ["Zeroth-Order Optimization"], "feature": "title_evidence"}, {"contribution": 0.04, "evidence": ["LLM", "language model", "large language model", "zeroth-order"], "feature": "contextual_evidence"}, {"contribution": 0.08, "evidence": ["Training", "Zeroth-Order"], "feature": "training_signal"}, {"contribution": 0.02, "evidence": ["arXiv (Cornell University)", "general_unlisted"], "feature": "venue_prestige"}, {"contribution": 0.08, "evidence": ["abstract"], "feature": "metadata_abstract"}, {"contribution": 0.03, "evidence": ["10.48550/arxiv.2610.26790"], "feature": "metadata_doi"}, {"contribution": 0.02, "evidence": ["https://openalex.org/W7223016913"], "feature": "metadata_openalex_id"}, {"contribution": 0.02, "evidence": ["2026", "arXiv (Cornell University)"], "feature": "metadata_venue_and_year"}, {"contribution": 0.05, "evidence": ["3_days"], "feature": "freshness"}], "selection_status": "summary_slot", "source_type": "openalex", "title": "Training with ML-labeled Data via Stochastic First- and Zeroth-Order Optimization", "venue": "arXiv (Cornell University)", "year": 2026}
